# Changes to these paths need the owner's review once "Require review from Code
# Owners" is on for main (see ci/README.md). They decide what CI runs and what a
# release publishes, without being part of the crate's source.

# Workflows, the release path and the scripts they run.
/.github/ @GrantSparks
/ci/ @GrantSparks
/scripts/ @GrantSparks

# Read by cargo and rustup in every job without being named anywhere. Cargo
# configuration can run programs and redirect registries, and the toolchain file
# selects the compiler; neither is part of the published crate.
/.cargo/ @GrantSparks
/rust-toolchain.toml @GrantSparks

# The dependency set and its exact versions. Every build script and procedural
# macro in the lockfile runs in the job that holds the SDK secrets, and the
# manifest lists the files a release publishes.
/Cargo.toml @GrantSparks
/Cargo.lock @GrantSparks
